<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93193" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαμβύκ-η</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ], ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a triangular musical instrument with four
			strings</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1341b1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Neanth.
				5
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, Juba <i><span class="en">
				73
			</span></i>; of barbaric origin, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.3.17
			</span></i>. (Aramaic <i>sabbekhā</i> (perh. not Semitic),
			with <i>m</i> inserted, as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμβακούμ</span>
			=
			<u>Habakkuk.</u> etc.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαμβυκίστρια</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.37.10
			</span></i>; with pun on signf. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				8.6.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>an engine of like form</i> used in sieges, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				8.4.8
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Bito
				57.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.Mech.
				27.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				26
			</span></i>.—Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάμβυξ</span>.
			[Penult. long in <i>sambūca</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pers.
				5.95
			</span></i>.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
